{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.199": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Sustainability Studies (3-year Limited Term)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Sustainability Studies (3-year Limited Term) - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Assistant Professor, Sustainability Studies (3-year Limited Term) School of Continuing Education Competition No. 26.08.199 Category Salary Closing Date Full-Time Limited Term Commensurate with qualifications and experience. The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Full-Time Limited Term Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience. Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity The School of Continuing Education invites applicants for the entry-level, full-time, three-year limited term appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, Sustainability Studies, commencing January 1, 2027 or as soon as possible after this date, subject to final budgetary approval. The successful applicant will hold a PhD (or evidence of near completion) with a focus on issues relating to sustainability education, theory, principles, and practices from an interdisciplinary perspective. Applicants should demonstrate a commitment to undergraduate education and provide evidence of teaching excellence, curriculum development and experience with teaching online at a post-secondary level. Preference will be given to candidates who incorporate work-integrated learning approaches in their courses as well as project and community-based approaches to teaching and learning. This is a teaching and service position at the Assistant Professor level with an expectation of a teaching workload of not more than 8 courses. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and teaching dossier (including recent teaching evaluations). Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted by the Associate Dean to provide three (3) letters of reference sent directly from referees and copies of official transcripts sent directly from the institution. Questions about this opportunity may be addressed to Eaman Mah, Associate Dean, School of Continuing Education, at mahe@macewan.ca . Further information about the program and the School of Continuing Education is available at: https://calendar.macewan.ca/programs/certificates-achievement/sustainability/#overviewtext How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.07.149": {
      "title": "Sessional Instructor",
      "description": "Sessional Instructor - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Sessional Instructor Department of Management and Organizations, School of Business Competition No. 26.07.149 Category Salary Closing Date Sessional Commensurate with qualifications. The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Sessional Salary Commensurate with qualifications. Closing Date The competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity The Department of Management and Organizations in the School of Business at MacEwan University is seeking sessional instructors to teach courses in Library and Information Technology for the upcoming academic year. Please visit the department’s website for a list of available courses: https://www.macewan.ca/academics/academic-departments/management-organizations/ Qualifications Applicants should hold a minimum of a Master's- or Professional-level degree in the relevant discipline or related fields, though the terminal degree is preferred. Post-secondary teaching experience, as well as professional experience in the field, is an asset: MacEwan University offers guidance and support to faculty in developing instructional skills and resources. You should submit a letter of interest and curriculum vitae. Include a list of courses you are qualified to teach and indicate during which terms (Fall, Winter, Spring/Summer) you would be available. Only selected candidates will be required to submit official transcripts sent directly from the institutions where you completed your degrees. Questions about this opportunity may be addressed to Dr. Noufou Ouedraogo, Chair, Department of Management and Organizations, ouedraogon@macewan.ca. How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.07.155": {
      "title": "Sessional Instructor, Perioperative Nursing Practice",
      "description": "Sessional Instructor, Perioperative Nursing Practice - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Sessional Instructor, Perioperative Nursing Practice Department of Professional Nursing and Allied Health, Faculty of Nursing Competition No. 26.07.155 Category Salary Closing Date Sessional Commensurate with qualifications. A review of applications will begin July 24, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. Category Sessional Salary Commensurate with qualifications. Closing Date A review of applications will begin July 24, 2026 and continue until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity The Department of Professional Nursing and Allied Health in the Faculty of Nursing invites applications for sessional faculty members to teach within the Perioperative Nursing Certificate for Registered Nurses and Licensed Practical Nurses. The Faculty of Nursing delivers excellent nursing education across four academic Departments and collectively offers various credentials including a Certificate in Perioperative Nursing for Registered Nurses and Licensed Practice Nurses. The Department of Professional Nursing and Allied Health provides students, nurses, and healthcare professionals with innovative learning opportunities designed to expand knowledge and increase expertise. Courses and programs in this department emphasize specific areas of continued learning, which are aligned with dynamic health care environments and responsive to health care education needs. For this specific opportunity you may teach across perioperative specific lecture, lab and clinical courses. Opportunities to teach other courses may also be available and travel may be required. Successful candidates will demonstrate enthusiasm for teaching, a student-centered approach to learning, and a strong understanding of perioperative nursing practice. You must have a baccalaureate nursing degree (Master’s preferred) with strong perioperative nursing experience and certification or formal education specific to perioperative practice (e.g. ORNAC certification). You will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in undergraduate and continuing education. Previous teaching experience is an asset. Applicants must have unencumbered licensure with the College of Registered Nurses of Alberta (CRNA) as well as meet the Requisite Skills and Abilities of the profession. You will submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume at the time of application. Only selected candidates will be contacted for an interview. Questions about this opportunity may be addressed to the Department Chair, Leanne Topola at TopolaL@macewan.ca. How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca. If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
    "https://www.macewan.ca/about-macewan/careers/opportunities/postings/?competition=26.08.178": {
      "title": "Sessional Instructors",
      "description": "Sessional Instructors - MacEwan University This website requires Javascript. To continue, enable Javascript in your browser settings and then reload this page. MENU myPortal Contact Us Safe at MacEwan Apply Visit Give Academics Apply & Enrol Campus Life About About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section Opportunities Pension, Benefits & Time Away Balance & Well-being Professional Development Working On Campus Faculty & Staff Agreements Contact Us About MacEwan Careers Opportunities Opportunity Details In This Section CAREERS Sessional Instructors Department of Accounting and Finance, Triffo School of Business Competition No. 26.08.178 Category Salary Closing Date Sessional Commensurate with Qualifications. This competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Category Sessional Salary Commensurate with Qualifications. Closing Date This competition will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. About Us MacEwan University is where caring faculty help people connect their passions to their future paths. Located in the heart of Edmonton's diverse and dynamic downtown community, and on the traditional lands of Treaty 6 First Nations and homelands of the Métis people, MacEwan is known for exceptional undergraduate learning. With its dedication to teaching excellence, informed by scholarly research, innovation, and creative activity, MacEwan provides an exceptional collaborative and supportive learning environment with a commitment to human rights, environmental sustainability, and opportunities for community engagement. We are committed to creating an equitable, diverse, inclusive, and welcoming community for all peoples, cultures, and identities. Our comprehensive undergraduate university offers 55 programs to more than 20,000 full- and part-time students in business, communications, community and human services, design, fine and performing arts, health, humanities, natural science, nursing, public safety, and social science. Through a wide array of experiential learning opportunities, and strategic relationships in the community, we partner with others to produce graduates of stature. Along with a robust grounding in their chosen disciplines, MacEwan students are given durable life skills that prepare them to take on the world. Opportunity The Department of Accounting and Finance in the Triffo School of Business at MacEwan University is seeking sessional instructors to teach courses in Accounting or Finance for the upcoming academic year. Please visit the Department’s website for a list of available courses: https://www.macewan.ca/academics/academic-departments/accounting-finance/academics/courses/ Qualifications Applicants should hold at minimum a CPA designation and a Master’s degree in Business, Accounting or related discipline. Evidence of effective post-secondary teaching as well as professional experience in the field is an asset: MacEwan University offers guidance and support to faculty in developing instructional skills and resources. You should submit a letter of interest and curriculum vitae. Include a list of courses you are qualified to teach and indicate during which terms (Fall, Winter, Spring/Summer) you would be available. Only selected candidates will be required to submit official transcripts sent directly from the institutions where you completed your degrees. Questions about this opportunity may be addressed to Dr. Greg Springate, Chair, Department of Accounting and Finance, springateg@macewan.ca. How to Apply To apply, please head to our MacEwan University Opportunities Page, select the job opportunity and click Apply Now. If you require assistance, please contact us at careers@macewan.ca . If you are experiencing technical difficulties when submitting your application, please try submitting through a different browser (i.e., Safari, Firefox, Chrome, etc.). If the issue persists, please send a screenshot of the error message to careers@macewan.ca so we can assist and ensure your application is received. This position is included under the Faculty Association collective agreement. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. This competition will remain open throughout the 2026-27 academic year. By applying to this competition, applicants acknowledge that their application may be considered for current and future vacancies of the same position classification that arise during the posting period. Apply Now Diversity Statement MacEwan University is committed to fostering the principles of equity, diversity, and inclusion within our community, and we are dedicated to removing barriers that have been historically encountered and are currently experienced by some members of our society. We welcome and encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized persons, visible minorities, women, persons with disabilities, sexual and gender minorities, and members of all equity-deserving groups. We believe that the diversity of our students, staff, and faculty serves as a strength of our institution and benefit to society. We are committed to ensuring full and inclusive participation for all in our community. Accessibility Statement We strive to provide an inclusive and barrier-free work environment, beginning with the hiring process. If you require accommodation, we want to ensure you have the support you need to showcase your abilities. Please contact humanresources@macewan.ca and we will support you to the best of our ability. Personal Information Collection Notification The personal information collected through MacEwan University’s application for employment and is used to determine your qualifications for employment. If your application progresses to the next stage of the hiring process, this information may be shared with non-HR members of the hiring committee and interview panel. This collection is authorized by section 4(c) of the Protection of Privacy Act. For questions about the collection of personal information, contact Human Resources at careers@macewan.ca or phone (780) 497-5434. Treaty Six Territory We acknowledge that the land on which we\n               gather in Treaty Six Territory is the traditional gathering\n               place for many Indigenous people.  We honour and respect the\n               history, languages, ceremonies and culture of the First \n               Nations, Métis and Inuit who call this territory home. Quick Links Feedback Privacy Careers Library #macewanu 10700 104 Ave NW Edmonton, AB T5J 4S2 info@macewan.ca MacEwan.ca/ContactUs"
    },
